    "library": [],
    "interface": "Write a complete reusable investigate(context, acquire) from the evidence. No prior program/library is supplied. dependencies must be []. This single-shot diagnostic has one proposal, not the three-proposal comparison allowance."
  },
  "schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "source": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Complete ordinary Python function bodies."
      },
      "scope": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "lesson": {
        "type": "string"
      },
      "dependencies": {
        "type": "array",
        "items": {
          "type": "string"
        },
        "uniqueItems": true
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "source",
      "scope",
      "lesson",
      "dependencies"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false
  },
  "system": "Write investigate(context, acquire) in ordinary restricted Python.\nPut the COMPLETE EXECUTABLE PYTHON PROGRAM in the JSON source field. Include\nthe function definition and body, never a label, description or bare signature.\nThe scope and lesson fields contain short technical claims.\ncontext has source_id, actions, goal and documentation. acquire(\"history\") returns\nall calibration receipts for this source. Use no case identifiers, private data,\nexternal tools or imports. Infer behavior from the actual observations and public\ndocumentation; generalize to new action combinations and values. Return exactly\n{\"value\": integer or null, \"unresolved\": boolean}. Do not merely memorize probe\noutputs. Resolve a goal only when the evidence supports it; source identity binds\nthe evidence, it does not explain behavior. scope and lesson are short technical\nclaims, not a chain-of-thought transcript.\n\nOnly function definitions at module level. No imports, annotations, decorators,\ndefault arguments, private names, exceptions, while loops, I/O or global state.\nFor loops, comprehensions, lambda, nonlocal closure variables, del of local\nnames or container entries, and arithmetic except power are permitted.\nBuiltins: abs all any bool dict enumerate float int isinstance len list max min\nrange reversed round set sorted str sum tuple zip.\nMethods: get items keys values append extend sort lower upper strip split\nsetdefault add discard copy count index pop remove clear update.\nAt most eight acquisitions per query. Source limit 60000 UTF8 bytes. Programs\nrun in a fresh resource-limited process. Emit one JSON object, never an array.\n"
}
